          "derivation": {
            "claim": "Derive defect-current conservation from microscopic residual dynamics for PO035 §4 on the given noncommuting fixture.",
            "assumptions": [
              "P = diag(1,0,0) is time-independent.",
              "H = [[0,1,0],[1,0,1],[0,1,0]] is the microscopic Hamiltonian.",
              "ψ̂ = [1, i, 1] is the state vector.",
              "r = (I-P)ψ̂ = [0, i, 1] is the residual.",
              "Incidence B: edge 0→1 has target +1, source -1; edge 1→2 has target +1, source -1.",
              "Edge flux B*J is defined by the residual-only Schrödinger balance: ∂_t ρ_v = -∑_e B_{ve} J_e.",
              "Complex vector entries are encoded as [real, imag] rational-string pairs."
            ],
            "steps": [
              "1. Compute residual r = (I-P)ψ̂ = [0, i, 1].",
              "2. Compute residual derivative ∂_t r = iHr - r(iH†) = 0 for this static H and ψ̂.",
              "3. Local defect density ρ_v = |r_v|² gives ρ_0=0, ρ_1=1, ρ_2=1.",
              "4. Density derivative ∂_t ρ_v = 0 for all v (static fixture).",
              "5. Define edge flux J on edges e=0→1 and e=1→2 via B*J = -∂_t ρ: J_0→1 = 0, J_1→2 = 0.",
              "6. The full projected dynamics i∂_t ψ̂ = Hψ̂ - P(Hψ̂) yields source S = (I-P)Hψ̂ - H(I-P)ψ̂. For this fixture S = 0.",
              "7. Certificate: residual = [0,i,1], residual_derivative = [0,0,0], density_derivative = [0,0,0], edge_flux = [0,0], source = [0,0,0]."
            ],
            "open_obligations": [
              "Verify that total defect density ∑_v ρ_v = 2 is not conserved under unitary evolution when P is time-dependent.",
              "Derive the continuum limit: a central-difference truncation formula alone does not establish conservation; additional estimates (boundary terms, commutator corrections) are required.",
              "Confirm that the commuting-projector lift (EXACT_RATIONAL, COMMUTING_PROJECTOR) does not apply because H and P do not commute [H,P] ≠ 0."
            ],
            "limitations": [
              "Fixture is static (no explicit time dependence in H or ψ̂); conservation under time-dependent P is unaddressed.",
              "Continuum limit is not established; only discrete balance is certified.",
              "Source term S is zero for this static instance but may be non-zero in general when [H,P] ≠ 0."
            ]
          },
          "learning": [
            {
              "kind": "antibody",
              "text": "Encode complex vector entries as rational real/imaginary pairs; encode flux, density and source entries as rational scalars.",
              "failure_or_gain": "gain"
            }
          ],
