              "reason": "Rational-string encoding of [real,imag] pairs and scalar entries is licensed."
            },
            {
              "id": "REFINEMENT_HYPOTHESES",
              "reason": "Explicit uniform refinement, time and coupling scaling hypotheses may be introduced as added, not derived."
            }
          ],
          "status": "PROPOSAL"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "summary": {
    "narrowest_defensible_thesis": "On the static noncommuting fixture with H=[[0,1,0],[1,0,1],[0,1,0]], P=diag(1,0,0), ψ̂=[1,i,1], the residual-only Schrödinger balance yields zero edge flux and zero source; total defect density ρ=2 is conserved in this instance but not guaranteed under time-dependent P or general [H,P]≠0.",
    "evidence_scope": "Discrete microscopic balance on the given fixture; continuum limit and time-dependent P conservation are open obligations.",
    "next_concrete_test": "Test conservation under time-dependent P and under unitary evolution of ψ̂ with [H,P]≠0; verify continuum limit with boundary-corrected truncation."
  }
